  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Ruth. You're verified. I found the earlier ticket. Yesterday's agent promised you $6.50 in account credit for the missing garlic knots on order Q-7690, but it was never applied.\n\nI've now added the $6.50 credit to your account, so your balance is $6.50. You can use it on a future order. I'm sorry for the delay.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thank you for finding that. I was told it would be $10, though, not $6.50. I don't have the order number handy, but it was yesterday's order from Big Slice Pizza. Could you check the ticket again to see if it says $10?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the ticket again. It records a promise of $6.50 in account credit for the garlic knots, and nothing about $10. That matches the price of the garlic knots on order Q-7690, which was $6.50. I can only honor what the record shows, so the $6.50 I added is the full amount.\n\nI can't add more credit for the same missing item, because it has already been compensated. If you'd like, I can pass this to a specialist who can review what you were told. Would you like that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I'm not sure about that. I remember the agent saying $10, but I could be mistaken, and I don't have anything in writing to show it. I'll take the $6.50 for now, since that's what the record shows. Thank you for your help."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Ruth. The $6.50 credit is on your account now and ready for your next order. Enjoy your meal, and have a good evening."
  }
